From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:20:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] Adjacency topologies and instance-rate attributes with
 geometry shaders

- Pipelines with a geometry shader and a *_WITH_ADJACENCY topology set the matching input
  primitive type (they were treated as the non-adjacency topology, so the geometry shader
  read half of its input vertices), and draws count primitives with the geometry shader's
  vertices per primitive (strips with adjacency: n - 3 lines, (n - 4) / 2 triangles), on
  the CPU and in the indirect-draw conversion kernel.
- DrawInfo gains vertexDivisors[] by Metal vertex buffer index (per-vertex or the instance
  divisor of VK_VERTEX_INPUT_RATE_INSTANCE bindings, including
  VkPipelineVertexInputDivisorStateCreateInfo), so the object stage fetches per-instance
  attributes by instance.
---
